# ------------------------------------------------------------
#  .env.example - copy this file to .env and fill in your own path.
#
#  .env is read by settings.py (via python-dotenv) and is listed in
#  .gitignore, so your path never ends up in git.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# The folder that holds YOUR private data. It must contain:
#   - Nordnet exports, found by name pattern (rename freely after the *):
#       Daglig udvikling*.csv     (Min konto > Afkast > Daglig udvikling > Eksporter)
#       transactions*.csv         (Transaktioner > Eksporter)
#       Aktietabel*.csv           (Beholdning > Eksporter) - only portfolio.py uses it
#   - rules.toml                  (start from demo_data/rules.toml and edit)
# The scripts create output\ (dashboard, reports, charts, CSVs) and
# rules_backup\ (dated copies made before the lookup page edits rules.toml)
# and cache\ (downloaded Yahoo data, so later runs only fetch what's new)
# inside this same folder.
#
# Write the path as is - no quotes needed, spaces are fine:
#   BEAT_SNP_DATA_DIR=C:\Users\me\Documents\portfolio-data
#
# Leave it empty (or delete .env) to run on the synthetic demo_data\ instead.
BEAT_SNP_DATA_DIR=
